# Wormy project context

The name of the character/player is Wormy.
8-bit Dizzy-style adventure: **Phaser 3** + **Tiled**, single entry point `main.js`, map at `Maps/wholemap.json`.

Run via local server (`python3 -m http.server 8080`) — `file://` breaks asset loading.

## World scale

- Tiles: **16×16 px**
- One screen: **24×13 tiles** (384×208 px); extend map width in multiples of 24
- Player sprite and physics body: **native 16×16** — do not scale sprites down (breaks Arcade body offsets/collisions)

## Tiled layers (tile layers)

| Layer | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `Background` | Visual scenery (ground, props, static art) |
| `Collisions` | Solid tiles — or any layer with property `collides=true` |
| `Hazards` | **All water**: animated surface + static body. Swimming + energy drain. No separate `Water` layer. |

**Water setup:** Paint the full pool on `Hazards`. Use animated water tile (tileset `water`, firstgid ~28) for the surface and static `Water` tile from `wormy_tiles` (tile id 6, gid ~27) for the body. Leave the water column **empty on `Collisions`** so the worm can enter. Energy drains at `WATER_ENERGY_DRAIN_PER_SEC` (10/s) while overlapping hazard tiles.

Phaser does not auto-play Tiled tile animations — animated water is driven manually in `_setupAnimatedMapTiles` / `_updateAnimatedMapTiles`.

## Tiled object layers

| Layer | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `Objects` | Optional `Spawn` object (else `DEFAULT_SPAWN_TILE` in `main.js`) |
| `Items` | Point objects with `itemType` matching `ITEM_DEFINITIONS`; optional `hiddenUntil` for stacked pickups |
| `Interactions` | Puzzle zones — see README for `action`, `requiredItem`, `target`, states |

## Tilesets

- `spelunky_shop`, `wormy_tiles`, `water` — see `TILESET_SPECS` in `main.js` for external `.tsx` normalization
- Export map as **JSON** (not `.tmx`); embedded tilesets in JSON work out of the box

## Code conventions

- Tune gameplay via top-of-file constants in `main.js` (physics, energy, layers, URLs)
- New puzzle behaviours: add handlers to `INTERACTION_HANDLERS`; new items: `ITEM_DEFINITIONS`
- Bump `main.js?v=…` in `index.html` when testing cache-sensitive changes
- Keep diffs minimal; match existing style; don't commit unless the user asks

